  "worked_solution": "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $4.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =4.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)+D\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =4$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{\u2033}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[16(D-Ct)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)-16(C+Dt)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)]+16t(C\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)+D\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)) & =5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t) \\\\ 16D\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)-16C\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t) & =5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=0$ and $D=\\frac{5}{8}.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t+\u03d5)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t+\u03d5)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t)$\n\nOnly solution II matches the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
